# What never reaches a build context, and therefore never reaches a server.
#
# Coolify builds from the git repository, where most of this is absent already.
# This file is for the other case — `docker build .` from a working tree — and
# the first entry is the reason it exists rather than a tidiness measure.

# Real customer data. `legacy/mirzabot-php/db/` holds the production MySQL dump:
# 11,241 Telegram identities, 4,629 payments, card numbers. It is gitignored, so
# it is only ever here, on this machine — and a build context is exactly how it
# would stop being only here.
legacy/

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image. Copying a Windows-built dist into a Linux image is
# how a stale asset ships without anyone choosing it.
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
graphify-out/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/

# Secrets. `sim/.env.local` carries the test bot token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
sim/.env.local

# The operator's own keys. `.notes/deploy_key` is the server's root SSH key and
# `.notes/deploy.env` holds the Coolify and Cloudflare tokens.
#
# Neither was excluded until 2026-08-21, and the patterns above look like they
# covered it: `.env.*` does not match `deploy.env`, and Docker patterns are not
# recursive, so `**/` is what makes the second line mean anything. `**/*.md`
# DID catch the notes beside them, which is what made the gap read as covered.
#
# Every `docker build .` from a working tree baked all three into the image
# layers, where `docker history` and `docker save` return them even if a later
# stage deletes the files.
.notes/
**/.notes/

# Screenshots. `coolify-pg.png` is a panel screenshot with a connection string
# in it; it is excluded from git by name, and nothing excluded it from here.
*.png
**/*.png

# Nothing in the image reads these.
docs/
**/*.md
!deploy/README.md
test-results
playwright-report
